## Scope and reproducibility notes

The main exported feature map has a linear output:

$$\phi_{\mathrm{main}}(x)=W_2\tanh(W_1x+b_1)+b_2.$$

The supplementary non-polynomial model has a tanh output:

$$\phi_{\mathrm{stress}}(x)=\tanh\!\left(W_2\tanh(W_1x)\right).$$

The manuscript's two-tanh Jacobian formula must use $D_2=I$ for the main export. The general radial theorem covers both choices. Details and additional correspondence notes are [recorded explicitly](docs/MANUSCRIPT_CODE_MAP.md).

For the main Monte Carlo experiment, the numerical failure event is

$$E_\tau=\left\{x:\|x\|_2^2>10^{-8},\quad \dot V(x)+0.15\|x\|_2^2>10^{-10}\right\}.$$

The deterministic grid contributes no binomial trials. Zero events in 200,000 IID trials give a one-sided 95% upper bound $p_U\approx1.498\times10^{-5}$ for this numerical event under uniform sampling. The non-polynomial grid excludes points with $\|x\|_2^2\le10^{-12}$; its sampled evidence has no continuum implication.

The theoretical robustness threshold uses $|\delta|$, and the two-system coupling condition is $|\kappa|<\frac{c}{2g}$. Both require an invariant sublevel inside the verified domain and sound bounds. The hard CLF filter requires feasibility; a positive soft slack alone gives no strict decrease guarantee.

